From 450f1ddf57dfab8417c93e22f58603806648afbd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:06:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] RomM Library: fix garbled text on the download and warning
 screens

Reported on the device: the app works, but the download progress and the warning
messages looked garbled while the menus were fine.

Those screens go through infoscreen.sh -> sdl2imgshow, which draws with
TTF_RenderText_Solid: the text is read as Latin-1 (not UTF-8) and nothing wraps.
The menus use selector/VirtualKeyboard, which read UTF-8.

- screen_text (lib/common.sh) + lib/screentext.awk + data/latin1.tsv: U+00A0..FF become one
  Latin-1 byte; curly quotes, dashes, ellipsis and Latin letters outside Latin-1 become ASCII;
  anything left (CJK) becomes "?"; lines are word-wrapped to 880 px estimated for the theme font.
  On any failure the original text is shown as before.
- used by ui_info, ui_wait, ui_confirm and the download progress screen.
- tests: the infoscreen mock keeps the raw bytes (info.raw) and the UTF-8 reading (info.log);
  15 new checks (109 -> 124), 5 of them fail with the old code.
- README and docs/HISTORICO-2026-11-22.md (section 10) updated.

Not verified on the device: only dash and mawk here, not the BusyBox awk/tr.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RhMAqBm84PVkwcVFZvG6f2
